Description: antinomie: keep the kernel's BTF type for type Debian's
 Built with Debian's configuration, the kernel's BTF has Debian's types,
 but pahole numbers them in the order it meets them and gives a function
 an entry whenever an ELF symbol of that name exists. Debian's modules
 carry BTF that refers to vmlinux's types by number, so they are valid on
 this kernel only if every type has the number Debian's build gave it.
 What moved types or added some:
 .
 - The embedded configuration (IKCONFIG, which the image builders read and
   Debian does not build) brought its module strings' array types in early.
   kernel/configs.o is built without debug information.
 - The recorder's process cores called fs/coredump.c's static helpers
   (coredump_wait(), dump_vma_snapshot(), vma_dump_size() and what they
   call) from a second place, so the compiler emitted them out of line, each
   a BTF function (and a traceable one) Debian's build does not have. The
   recorder now runs its own copies of them (kernel/antinomie/core_writer.c,
   from Linux 6.12.94); fs/coredump.c keeps its hooks and a reader of
   kernel.core_sort_vma, and declares only opaque accessors.
 - The transport's per-CPU producer state was a static per-CPU variable,
   which moved every later per-CPU variable of the kernel (their offsets
   are in BTF's .data..percpu section): it is allocated at setup
   (alloc_percpu()), in the contract copy of guest.c too.
 - io_xattr_finish(), __io_setxattr_prep() and io_waitid_finish() grew with
   the recorder's hooks and were no longer inlined: they are
   __always_inline, as Debian's build inlines them.
 - Recorder functions named like stock ones (put_event, remove_one,
   event_release) gave pahole a symbol for a stock function Debian inlines,
   or two symbols for one name. They are renamed, and so are the copies in
   core_writer.c.
 .
 With Debian's configuration the kernel's BTF is then byte for byte the BTF
 of Debian's own 6.12.94-1 image (the BTF filter keeps the strings pahole
 leaves unused, as Debian's has them).
 .
 Hooked kernel files: kernel/Makefile; io_uring/xattr.c and
 io_uring/waitid.c (inline attributes); fs/coredump.c loses code.
Author: MikiMiku <jonathanirvinjo@gmail.com>
Origin: project
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-29

